# Project

Frontend capstone app (TypeScript strict mode). Use npm and current Node LTS.

## Stack

- **TypeScript** (strict mode)
- **React 18** with **Vite**
- **Tailwind CSS** for styling
- **Vitest** + React Testing Library for tests

## Commands

- `npm install` — dependencies
- `npm run dev` — dev server
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run test` — unit tests
- `npm run lint` — lint

## Source layout (`src/`)

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `components/` | Reusable UI components |
| `pages/` | Route-level screens |
| `hooks/` | Custom React hooks |
| `lib/` | Helpers, API clients, utilities |
| `types/` | Shared TypeScript types |
| `styles/` | Global styles |

Also: `assets/` (images, fonts, icons). Unit tests co-locate as `Component.test.tsx`; broader tests live in `tests/`.

## Code conventions

- Functional components and hooks only; no class components.
- One component per file; PascalCase filenames (`SearchBar.tsx`).
- Prefer **named exports** over default exports.
- Keep components small; extract logic into hooks (`useThing.ts`).
- No **`any`**; use `unknown` and narrow, or proper types.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, labels on inputs, visible focus states.

## Git (Conventional Commits)

Messages follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `type(scope): summary`.

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`.

- Imperative mood; summary under 72 characters.
- Small, focused commits; work on feature branches; keep `main` working.
- Never commit secrets or `.env` files.
